<p>
Nudged by Ihor Radchenko's suggestion, I added some JavaScript to translate the graphical SVG schedule on the EmacsConf wiki to your local time zone.
I'll post the schedule on the wiki next week, but in the meantime, you can take a look at the <a href="https://emacsconf.org/2026/organizers-notebook/#draft-schedule">draft schedule</a> in the organizers' notebook.
</p>

<p>
Let me test it by setting my local time zone to UTC with <code>sudo timedatectl set-timezone Etc/UTC</code>&hellip;
</p>


