<p>
I still need to make sure that my time zone is set to America/Toronto when I'm  generating the SVGs, but at least now people can see the times translated to their local time zone.
</p>

<p>
The Javascript code is in <a href="https://emacsconf.org/script.js">https://emacsconf.org/script.js</a> as <code>addLocalTimeToSVGs</code>.
The Emacs Lisp code to generate these SVGs is in <a href="https://git.emacsconf.org/emacsconf-el/tree/emacsconf-schedule.el">emacsconf-schedule.el</a>. <code>emacsconf-schedule-svg</code> is the starting point.
</p>
